2. **On launchd, `status` does not show which home the installed job serves. So Step 8's consent is uninformed in the case the plan itself worries about.** Probe: `/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mobaxterm-worktrees-Texarkanine-stockroom-stockroom-claudeboarding/3b628427-7950-4f51-90b9-cfcc5ad0911b/scratchpad/preflight-r4b/scripts/status_home_visibility_probe.py`. It installs for home A (`…/Library/Application Support/stockroom`), then runs status as a shell that resolves home B (the default).
    - cron: the `installed:` line shows `STOCKROOM_HOME='<A>'`, and `log:` shows B. The agent can name both to the user.
    - launchd: `installed: nightly at 03:30 (jp.ne.cani.stockroom.nightly)`, `up-to-date: no`, `log: <B>`. Nothing names A.
