6. **Make-test hardening.** The Unit 3 tests rely on `UV=` alone to keep the real `uv` out of the recipes. If a recipe ever bypassed `$(UV)`, `make local-dashboard` would run the real `stockroom dashboard --replace` and replace the operator's live dashboard. Also put the `stub_uv` bin dir first on the subprocess `PATH`. Today no recipe bypasses `$(UV)`: the poison `uv` was never called.
7. **Inventory 2 should state where its search stopped.** It lists the engine's own `os.environ` reads. cron and launchd also drop variables that libraries read. Examples are `HF_HOME`, where `sentence-transformers` caches the embedding model, and uv's `UV_*` settings. With a custom `HF_HOME`, the first nightly embed downloads the model again into `~/.cache/huggingface`. That does not break the job, so it is out of scope by the operator's rule. But the inventory claims every variable the nightly job needs, so it should name this boundary.

